# Avoid `any`, `unknown`, and bare `object` in JSDoc (checkJs)

Runtime code is plain `.js` with `checkJs`. **Do not use `any`, `unknown`, or bare `object` / `Object` as lazy escape hatches** in `@param`, `@returns`, `@property`, or `@type`. Name the real shape.

Pair with [`jsdoc-import-types.mdc`](jsdoc-import-types.mdc) — import types at the top with `@import`, not inline `import()`.

## Prefer

- **Shared typedefs** — co-located `*-types.js` or exported shapes from `@qctl/shared`
- **`@import`** then compose with `Pick`, `Omit`, `ReturnType`, unions, literals
- **Parse / narrow at boundaries** — YAML, env, subprocess stdout → validate once, then pass concrete types inward
- **Type guards** — `isFoo(value): value is Foo` instead of `/** @param {unknown} */`

## Don't

```js
// BAD — erases type safety
/** @param {any} payload */
/** @param {unknown} value */
/** @param {object} doc */
/** @returns {Record<string, unknown>} */
/** @type {unknown} */
/** @type {object} */
function handle(data) { ... }
```

## Named shapes vs bare `object`

`@typedef {object} Foo` **with** `@property` lines is fine — that *defines* a concrete named type:

```js
/**
 * @typedef {object} SyncOptions
 * @property {string} root
 * @property {boolean} [dryRun]
 */
```

Never use bare `{object}` alone as a parameter or return type.

## When `unknown` is acceptable

Use sparingly and **only at the outer edge** — never as the main type for domain objects:

| Case | Pattern |
|------|---------|
| `catch` | `catch (error)` then narrow (`error instanceof Error`) |
| Third-party / opaque blob before parse | Local variable, immediately validated; don't export `unknown` APIs |
| Truly opaque external value | One-line cast **after** a guard, with a short comment explaining why |

Bare `object` is **not** an acceptable substitute — still name the fields or use a typedef.

If you reach for `any` / `unknown` / bare `object`, stop: add or reuse a typedef or guard instead.
